     "<div class=\"gmail_extra\"><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div><div><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div class=\"gmail_extra\"><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><span><div dir=\"ltr\">I have created a shiny app that takes as input multiple result files from different models. The user can browse folders and upload the files, then they can then chose which model to plot, filter the plot, and search in the result file. <div>The app works fine on my computer (windows 7), as well as two other PCs (windows 7 and debian), but it does not seem to work on two other windows 7. On the first one &quot;browse&quot; (fileInput) is not working at all, while on the second PC it uploads the files and that&#39;s about it, the results are not plotted. On the 3 &quot;working&quot; PCs the R versions are all different, as well as the java versions, so this doesn&#39;t seem to be an issue. All R versions on all PCs meet the requirement of R &gt;=3.0.0</div><div><br></div><div>I am not sure why is this happening and where to look for a solution. </div><div>Any advice would be greatly appreciated.</div><div><br></div></div>\r\n\r\n<p></p>\r\n\r\n-- <br></span>\r\nYou received this message because you are subscribed to the Google Groups &quot;Shiny - Web Framework for R&quot; group.<br></blockquote></div></blockquote></div></div></blockquote></div></div></div></blockquote></div></div>"
